
%9Syntax:%9

SKANER %|[<channel>]
SKANER ALL%|
SKANER ON%|
SKANER OFF%|
SKANER STATUS%|
SKANER HELP%|

%9Parameters:%9

    ALL:         Report for all channels of the active window's server.
    ON:          Turns automatic reports and alerts on (skaner_enabled).
    OFF:         Turns automatic reports and alerts off.
    STATUS:      Version, state and number of channels on all servers.
    HELP:        Short help.

    A channel on the active window's server; without an argument, the
    channel in the active window.

%9Description:%9

    Looks for clones on a channel (several nicks with the same host, i.e.
    the part after '@', case-insensitive) and for IRC operators (the '*'
    flag in the WHO reply). A command of the skaner.pl script.

    Everything - reports, alerts and error messages - goes to a separate
    window (by default "skaner"), not to the window where the command was
    typed. The window is created in the background at startup, has
    /WINDOW IMMORTAL on, and is recreated by the script if it gets closed.

    A report contains: a header (channel, network, number of users), clone
    groups from the largest (count, host, nicks with @ %% + prefixes, at
    most 12, the rest as +N), IRC operators with their hosts, and the
    number of users with no known host (e.g. when WHO was skipped because
    of channel_max_who_sync).

    With skaner_enabled = ON a report is produced automatically after you
    join a channel, once erssi has finished syncing it; a channel with no
    findings then gives a single line (or nothing with
    skaner_show_clean = OFF). When someone whose host is already present
    joins a synced channel, a clone alert appears in the skaner window
    (level NOTICES - the window gets an activity mark). A manual /SKANER
    always gives the full report.

%9Settings:%9

    skaner_enabled = ON
        Automatic reports after joining a channel, and clone alerts.
    skaner_show_clean = ON
        One line also for channels with no findings (automatic report).
    skaner_window = skaner
        Name of the window for the results.

%9Examples:%9

    /SKANER
    /SKANER #channel
    /SKANER ALL
    /SKANER OFF

%9See also:%9 NAMES, WHO, WINDOW

